+// The CPU backend is kept as the owner of GS local memory: uploads, transfers,
+// the CLUT and presentation all still go through it. Render targets are mirrored
+// on the GPU and written back to local memory only when something reads them
+// (presentation, a transfer, a texture that isn't the target itself), and
+// reloaded when something else writes their pages.
