+// Builds the schedule of the straight-line block starting at a pair, with the
+// dynamic model's rules (calculatePairReadyCycle / markPairWrites) applied to
+// cycle offsets from block entry. Registers not written earlier in the block
+// are assumed ready at entry; each such read becomes a live-in that
+// staticEntryOk checks, so a block only runs statically when this schedule
+// is exactly what the dynamic loop would produce. The block ends after a
+// branch's delay slot, after the pair following an E-bit, at a D/T-bit pair
+// or after 64 pairs.
+void VU1Interpreter::buildStaticBlock(StaticBlock &block, const uint8_t *vuCode, uint32_t codeSize, uint32_t startIndex)
+{
